WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.790
After half a decade of build-up, The Rise
of Skywalker has finally introduced Rey's

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.860
parents, one of whom is a familiar face to
fans of prestige television.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.339
Here's why Rey's mother in The Rise of Skywalker
looks so familiar.

00:00:12.339 --> 00:00:16.130
It may just be a brief flashback moment, but
Jodie Comer's appearance as Rey's mom in the

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:21.009
final film in the Skywalker saga is a pretty
huge deal for the 26-year-old Liverpool-born

00:00:21.009 --> 00:00:23.490
actress, who's primarily worked in British
TV.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.710
After getting her start in theatre as a young
actress, Comer worked a series of odd jobs,

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:31.130
including as a checkout girl at Britain's
Tesco chain of supermarkets, before finally

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:35.770
booking her first television gig in a 2008
guest role on medical soap The Royal Today,

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.300
a spin-off of the popular ITV series The Royal.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:43.390
From there, Comer went on to appear on shows
like Law &amp; Order: UK, Vera, Doctors, Casualty,

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:47.680
and more, before booking a plum role on My
Mad, Fat Diary in 2013.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.320
Based on Rae Earl's novel My Fat, Mad Teenage
Diary, the E4 series featured Comer as Chloe,

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.820
the popular, pretty childhood best friend
of the show's main character Rachael, played

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:56.820
by Sharon Rooney.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.460
Overall, My Mad, Fat Diary received critical
acclaim and even several BAFTA nominations,

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.800
putting Comer on a path to stardom.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.660
"And, well, you know the rest!"

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.060
From there, Comer built up her resume by appearing
on several acclaimed miniseries produced through

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:16.220
BBC, including BBC Three's Thirteen, which
earned Comer a nomination for Best Actress

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:19.690
at the British Academy Television Awards,
and Rillington Place.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.960
Some of the series eventually made their way
across the pond to the U.S., where Comer's

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.890
profile is steadily rising.

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:29.300
Comer was no stranger to historical dramas
and period pieces; in 2015, she appeared in

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:34.840
an adaptation of the classic novel Lady Chatterley's
Lover on BBC One, but 2017's The White Princess

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.020
was the first big stepping stone in her career.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.890
A sequel to BBC and Starz's miniseries The
White Queen, which starred Mission: Impossible's

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:45.220
Rebecca Ferguson as Elizabeth Woodville, a
commoner who marries King Edward IV and becomes

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:48.920
queen, The White Princess tells the story
of Elizabeth of York, the daughter of Edward

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:53.140
and Woodville who marries Henry Tudor and
eventually mothers Henry VIII, one of England's

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.380
bloodiest and most notorious monarchs.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.640
Both series are based on books by Philippa
Gregory, a prominent historical fiction author.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.049
"A puppet for my mother's own ambition.

00:02:03.049 --> 00:02:07.854
It was her who craved the throne for me."

00:02:07.854 --> 00:02:12.140
The White Princess gave Comer a chance to
show her considerable range as Elizabeth ascends,

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:15.870
somewhat unwillingly, to the throne alongside
her new husband, who's considered by most

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:16.930
to be a usurper.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:20.329
But even those who had been following Jodie
Comer for years were unprepared for what was

00:02:20.329 --> 00:02:22.510
to come for the vibrant young actress.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:26.569
The most important role of Jodie Comer's career
thus far arrived shortly after her turn on

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:27.620
The White Princess.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:32.299
In June 2017, she scored the part of Russian
assassin and verifiable psychopath Villanelle

00:02:32.299 --> 00:02:34.170
on the BBC series Killing Eve.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.950
On the show, which was created by Fleabag's
Phoebe Waller-Bridge, Villanelle is a fabulous

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:42.349
yet frightening contract killer who develops
a fascination with Sandra Oh's Eve, an MI6

00:02:42.349 --> 00:02:43.530
agent tracking her whereabouts.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:47.780
As the two powerful women dance around each
other, leaving a bloody trail in their wake,

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:50.519
the drama and connection between them only
deepens.

00:02:50.519 --> 00:02:54.060
"I think you're going to bleed to death."

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.420
"What?"

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:59.159
Comer beat out more than 100 other actresses
to win the role of Villanelle, and her efforts

00:02:59.159 --> 00:03:00.779
clearly paid off handsomely.

00:03:00.779 --> 00:03:04.950
Thanks to her layered, terrifying performance,
which also requires the use of numerous accents

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:08.959
and languages, Comer has skyrocketed to fame,
earning a spot on The Hollywood Reporter's

00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:10.549
list of rising stars in 2018.

00:03:10.549 --> 00:03:15.540
"I shot him twice in the heart and watched
the spark drain from his eyes."

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:19.249
Both Comer and Oh, the latter of whom returned
to the small screen after years on ABC's hit

00:03:19.249 --> 00:03:22.849
drama series Grey's Anatomy, have won multiple
awards for their work on Killing Eve.

00:03:22.849 --> 00:03:28.870
Oh won a Golden Globe for Best Actress, Television
Series Drama in 2018, a SAG Award in 2019,

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.299
and multiple Emmy nods.

00:03:30.299 --> 00:03:33.749
As for Comer, she scored the top prize of
Outstanding Lead Actress in a Drama Series

00:03:33.749 --> 00:03:35.659
at the 2019 Emmy Awards.

00:03:35.659 --> 00:03:40.069
Comer herself and the series as a whole also
scored nominations for the 2020 Golden Globe

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:42.819
Awards, which will air on January 5, 2020.

00:03:42.819 --> 00:03:45.709
Of course, Comer will appear on the third
season of Killing Eve.

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:49.359
There's no release date yet, but so far, the
show has added other familiar faces to the

00:03:49.359 --> 00:03:54.189
cast, including Game of Thrones' Gemma Whelan
and Succession's Dame Harriet Walter.

00:03:54.189 --> 00:03:58.129
Now that Comer has earned enough fame and
acclaim to snag a coveted Star Wars cameo,

00:03:58.129 --> 00:04:02.180
there's nowhere she can go but up, and her
next role has a pretty high profile as well.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:06.599
In July 2020, Comer will appear in Shawn Levy's
Free Guy alongside a star-studded cast that

00:04:06.599 --> 00:04:11.230
includes Ryan Reynolds, Thor: Ragnarok director
Taika Waititi, and Stranger Things' Joe Keery,

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.230
and more.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:15.980
The film focuses on an NPC character in a
video game, Guy, who must figure out how to

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.440
crack the code of the game before his entire
world is erased.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.489
"I'm not gonna be the good guy.

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:22.019
I'm gonna be the great guy."

00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:23.210
"Okay.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:26.540
Well, enjoy your lifetime supply of virginity!"

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:31.050
Comer's star is clearly on the rise, and despite
her tiny role as Rey's mother in The Rise

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:35.449
of Skywalker, fans of Killing Eve, White Princess,
and any of her smaller roles likely clocked

00:04:35.449 --> 00:04:37.409
the distinctive actress right away.

00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:41.500
The role of Rey's mother was brief but also
incredibly pivotal, so in the end, it makes

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:45.699
sense that the powers that be at Lucasfilm
would want to cast such a powerful performer.

00:04:45.699 --> 00:04:49.370
Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker is in theaters
now, and the first two seasons of Killing

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:51.660
Eve are both currently streaming on Hulu.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:56.580
Catch Jodie Comer on the big screen once more
when Free Guy hits cinemas on July 3, 2020.

